expected `(&tensor[4, f64]) -> tensor[4, f64]`, got `(&tensor[4, f64]) -> List Option f64`

Pins the rule src/rolling.ch states: a tensor element is a precision type and
has no inhabitant for "absent", so the fifteen Option-returning tensor forms
return a list. Only tensor_shift_fill and tensor_shift_clamped, whose results
have no absent position, return a tensor.
